+# Pre-ship review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Reviewed: `packages/nextjs` frontend + config, against the deployed `Payouts` contract
+(`0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`, Base 8453).
+`tsc --noEmit` passes. Report only — no code was changed.
+
+Summary: **13 ship-blocking**, **9 should-fix**. The payouts page itself is the weak spot:
+the wallet flow has no disconnected/wrong-network states, writes bypass the scaffold hook, all
+errors are swallowed to the console, and the USDC entry lives in a file that the next
+`yarn deploy` overwrites.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. USDC is registered in `deployedContracts.ts` and will be wiped on the next deploy
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50` (and `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts:14`, empty)
+
+`deployedContracts.ts` is autogenerated. The hand-added `USDC` entry disappears the first time
+anyone runs `yarn deploy`, and after that `useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC" })`
+silently returns nothing — the balance read dies with no error, and the page's static
+`deployedContracts[8453].USDC` import stops type-checking.
+
+**Fix:** move the entry to `externalContracts.ts` and revert `deployedContracts.ts` to generated state:
+
+```typescript
+// packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: { address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913", abi: [/* existing ABI */] },
+  },
+} as const;
+```
+
+Then confirm `yarn next:check-types` still passes.
+
+### 2. Disconnected users get a paragraph, not a Connect button
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+
+```tsx
+{!isConnected ? (
+  <p className="mt-4">Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p>
+) : (
+```
+
+The user is told to connect and given nothing to click; the only connect affordance is in the
+header, off in the corner.
+
+**Fix:** render the real button in the action slot:
+
+```tsx
+import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+if (!isConnected) return <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton />;
+```
+
+### 3. No wrong-network branch on the primary action
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+A wallet connected to (say) Ethereum mainnet sees a fully live "Approve" / "Send Payout" pair.
+Clicking sends the write to the wrong chain: `useWriteContract` has no `chainId`, so it uses
+the wallet's current chain, the call reverts or hits a non-existent address, and the `catch`
+only logs (see #6). The header's `WrongNetworkDropdown` does not prevent this.
+
+**Fix:** gate the CTA on `useAccount().chain?.id !== targetNetwork.id` and replace it with a
+switch button:
+
+```tsx
+const { targetNetwork } = useTargetNetwork();
+const { switchChain } = useSwitchChain();
+if (chain?.id !== targetNetwork.id)
+  return <button className="btn btn-primary" onClick={() => switchChain({ chainId: targetNetwork.id })}>
+    Switch to {targetNetwork.name}
+  </button>;
+```
+
+(Switching to `useScaffoldWriteContract` per #4 also pins the chain id, which is a second layer
+of the same protection — do both.)
+
+### 4. Writes use raw wagmi `useWriteContract`, not `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:21`, used at `:38` and `:51`
+
+Raw `writeContractAsync` resolves as soon as the wallet returns a hash — **not** at confirmation.
+So `handlePay` clears the form (`:57-58`) while the tx is still pending, and the UI has no idea
+whether the payout actually landed. It also skips scaffold's pre-flight simulation, the
+tx-progress notifications, and the block-explorer link.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+const { writeContractAsync: writeUsdc, isMining: isApproving } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "USDC" });
+const { writeContractAsync: writePayouts, isMining: isPaying } = useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" });
+
+await writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parseUnits(amount, 6), memo] });
+```
+
+This also lets you drop the `deployedContracts` direct imports at `:10-11`.
+
+### 5. Approve and Send Payout are both live at once, with no allowance read
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+`Payouts.pay` calls `usdc.transferFrom(msg.sender, ...)`, so it reverts without an allowance.
+Nothing in the page reads `USDC.allowance`, so a first-time user's obvious move — click
+"Send Payout" — always fails, and there is no visible error explaining why (#6).
+
+**Fix:** read the allowance and render exactly one CTA:
+
+```tsx
+const { data: allowance, refetch: refetchAllowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+  functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, PAYOUTS_ADDRESS],
+});
+const needsApproval = (allowance ?? 0n) < parseUnits(amount || "0", 6);
+```
+
+Show Approve when `needsApproval`, otherwise Send Payout — never both. Call `refetchAllowance()`
+after the approve confirms.
+
+### 6. Every failure is silent — `catch (e) { console.error(e) }`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46` and `:59-61`
+
+A rejected signature, an insufficient balance, a missing allowance, a malformed recipient — all
+of them land in the console and the UI does nothing. To the user the button just... does nothing.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+import { notification, getParsedError } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+// ...
+} catch (e) {
+  notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+}
+```
+
+(Scaffold's own hook already notifies on simulation failure, so #4 covers part of this — but keep
+the explicit catch for wallet rejections.)
+
+### 7. Recipient is a raw `<input type="text">` — no ENS, no validation
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`, cast blindly at `:55`
+
+`recipient as \`0x${string}\`` is a lie to the type system. `vitalik.eth` never resolves,
+a typo'd or truncated address throws deep inside viem, and the error is swallowed by #6. On a
+real-money payouts form this is the highest-consequence input on the page.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+import { AddressInput } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="Recipient address or ENS" />
+```
+
+### 8. Event feed scans Base from block 0
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:32` — `fromBlock: 0n`
+
+Base is past 33.7M blocks. This asks the RPC to walk the entire chain history on every page
+load, then re-polls with `watch: true`. On the public/default endpoint (#14) it will rate-limit
+or time out, and "Latest payouts" renders as the empty state — which reads to the user as
+"my payout didn't go through".
+
+**Fix:** start from the deploy block already recorded in `deployedContracts.ts`
+(`deployedOnBlock: 33712450`):
+
+```tsx
+fromBlock: 33712450n,
+```
+
+### 9. Hardcoded black page wrapper breaks light mode and the theme switch
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65` — `className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white"`
+
+Light-mode users get a black page glued under the app's light header and footer, and the
+footer's `<SwitchTheme/>` visibly does nothing on this page. The `border-gray-700` at `:121`
+has the same problem in reverse (invisible on white).
+
+**Fix:** `className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content"`, and `border-base-300` on the
+feed rows.
+
+### 10. `loading` class on the buttons erases their labels
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101` and `:108`
+
+`btn loading` in DaisyUI replaces the button content with a spinner — mid-transaction both
+buttons become unlabelled circles, so the user can't tell which action is in flight.
+
+**Fix:** keep the text and add an inline spinner:
+
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isMining} onClick={handleApprove}>
+  {isMining && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm" />}
+  Approve
+</button>
+```
+
+### 11. Buttons gate on `isPending`, which clears mid-flight
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:102`, `:109`
+
+`isPending` from wagmi drops the moment the wallet hands back a hash — i.e. while the tx is still
+unconfirmed. The button re-enables and a user who doesn't see immediate feedback double-sends a
+payout. Real money, no idempotency on the contract side.
+
+**Fix:** use `isMining` from `useScaffoldWriteContract` (#4); it is held across
+`waitForTransactionReceipt` and cleared in the hook's `finally`. Gate each button on its own
+flag, not one shared one. If the allowance refetch needs an extra hold, keep it in local state
+and clear it in `finally` — never on a timer.
+
+### 12. Tab title, description and manifest still say "Scaffold-ETH 2"
+**Files:** `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:11-12`, `packages/nextjs/utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8`,
+`packages/nextjs/public/manifest.json`
+
+Users shipping this week get a browser tab reading "Scaffold-ETH 2 App", and every shared link
+previews as "Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2".
+
+**Fix:** set `title: "USDC Payouts"` / a real description in `layout.tsx`, change `titleTemplate`
+in `getMetadata.ts:8` to `"%s | USDC Payouts"`, update `manifest.json`, and replace
+`public/favicon.png` + `public/thumbnail.jpg` with product assets.
+
+### 13. The home page is still the untouched scaffold template
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx:20-45`
+
+`/` — the first thing a real user hits — says "Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2", tells them to edit
+`packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx`, references `YourContract.sol`, and links to the local-only Block
+Explorer. It doesn't mention payouts at all.
+
+**Fix:** replace with a short product landing (what the app does + a link to `/payouts`), or
+redirect `/` to `/payouts`. Drop the "Debug Contracts" and "Block Explorer" cards.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 14. Production RPC is the shared default Alchemy key
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:16,29,32-35`
+
+`rpcOverrides` is empty and `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` is blank in `.env.example`, so unless
+it's set on Vercel the app falls back to `DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` — a key shared by every SE-2
+project on the internet — and then to the bare `http()` public endpoint
+(`services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20`). Combined with #8 this is a rate-limit waiting to happen.
+
+**Fix:** provision a project-owned Base RPC and wire it through:
+
+```typescript
+rpcOverrides: { [chains.base.id]: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL as string },
+```
+
+Then **verify the variable is actually set in the Vercel production environment**, not just
+referenced in code.
+
+### 15. `pollingInterval: 30000` on an L2
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`
+
+Base blocks every ~2s. A 30s poll means a balance or payout feed that lags half a minute behind
+reality — the app feels broken right after a user sends money.
+
+**Fix:** drop to `~3000`, and refetch balance/allowance explicitly after each confirmation rather
+than relying on the poll.
+
+### 16. Default WalletConnect project ID
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:40`
+
+Hardcoded fallback `3a8170812b534d0ff9d794f19a901d64` is SE-2's shared demo ID — shared relay
+quota, and your app's name/icon in wallet prompts is whatever that project says.
+
+**Fix:** register your own at cloud.reown.com, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` in
+Vercel, and set `appName` in `services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:49` to "USDC Payouts" (currently
+`"scaffold-eth-2"`, which is the string users see in the connect prompt).
+
+### 17. Phantom users cannot connect
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:20-28`
+
+Phantom ships a large EVM user base on Base and is absent from the wallet list.
+
+**Fix:** `import { phantomWallet } from "@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/wallets"` and add it to `wallets`.
+
+### 18. No wallet redirect on mobile WalletConnect
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62`
+
+On a phone connected over WalletConnect, tapping Approve/Send fires the write and then nothing
+visible happens — the user has to remember to switch to their wallet app themselves. A meaningful
+share of mobile payouts will be abandoned here.
+
+**Fix:** after calling the write (never before — navigating away first means the write never
+fires), deep-link to the connected wallet, and skip it when already inside a wallet's in-app
+browser.
+
+### 19. Payout amounts are hand-rolled at 6 decimals with no balance check
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:42`, `:55`, `:85-91`
+
+`parseUnits(amount || "0", 6)` hardcodes USDC's decimals rather than reading `USDC.decimals`,
+and nothing compares the amount against `usdcBalance`. `type="number"` also lets the user type
+`1e5` and scroll-wheel the value while focused. An over-balance payout reverts on-chain — after
+the user has already paid gas for the approve.
+
+**Fix:** use `<IntegerInput>` or a validated text input, disable the CTA when
+`parsedAmount > usdcBalance` or `parsedAmount === 0n` with an inline "Insufficient balance"
+message, and source decimals from the contract.
+
+### 20. The Payouts contract address is never shown
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:64-76`
+
+The page asks users to grant a USDC allowance to a contract it never names. There is no way for
+a cautious user to check what they're approving.
+
+**Fix:** render it under the header:
+
+```tsx
+<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} chain={targetNetwork} />
+```
+
+### 21. Hand-rolled `shorten()` instead of `<Address/>`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:13`, used at `:122` and `:124`
+
+The feed loses ENS names, blockies, copy-to-clipboard and Basescan links — all things a payouts
+log specifically wants.
+
+**Fix:** `<Address address={payout.args.from} chain={targetNetwork} size="sm" />` and delete
+`shorten`. While there, key the list on `${log.transactionHash}-${log.logIndex}` rather than the
+array index (`:121`), which reshuffles as `watch: true` prepends new events.
+
+### 22. Pill-shaped inputs from `--radius-field: 9999rem`
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36` and `:63`
+
+Fully-rounded fields clip long content — which on this page is a 42-character address and a
+free-text memo.
+
+**Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in **both** `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks (theme level,
+not per-component `rounded-*`).
+
+### 23. Debug Contracts tab ships in production navigation
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx:28-32`
+
+A raw ABI console pointed at the live Base contract, one click away for every end user. Not a
+security hole (it can only do what the contract allows), but it's developer furniture in a
+product shipping to non-developers.
+
+### 24. Footer is still all BuidlGuidl / scaffold links
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/components/Footer.tsx:50-74`
+
+"Fork me" → the SE-2 repo, "Support" → the SE-2 Telegram. Users with a payout problem land in a
+channel that cannot help them.
+
+**Fix:** point Support at your own channel and drop or relabel "Fork me". Keep the BuidlGuidl
+attribution if you want it — just make Support real.
+
+### 25. README is the unmodified Scaffold-ETH 2 readme
+**File:** `README.md:1-20`
+
+Describes the starter kit, not the payouts dApp — no mention of the deployed contract address,
+the Base deployment, or required env vars.
+
+---
+
+## To confirm before ship (not code)
+
+- **Contract verification.** There is no `packages/hardhat/deployments/` directory in the repo, so
+  I can't confirm `Payouts` at `0x7c3f…b6F2` is verified on Basescan. Run `yarn verify --network base`
+  and check the explorer shows source. Unverified bytecode on a contract users grant USDC
+  allowance to is a trust problem, not just a nicety.
+- **Vercel env vars.** `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID`
+  are empty in `.env.example`; confirm they're populated in the production environment (see #14, #16).
+- **`NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR`** (`packages/nextjs/next.config.ts:6-8`) must not be `"true"`
+  on the production build. Types currently pass cleanly, so there's no reason for it to be set.

